{title: Samaria After Shemer}
{subtitle: 1 Kings 16:23–28}
{key: C}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [C] | [F] | [G] [C] [G/B] | [Am7] [F] |
| [G] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
In the [C]thir-ty-first [G/B]year of Asa's [Am]reign
[F]Omri took his [G]seat upon the [C]throne
[F]He ruled for [G]twelve years in the [C]land
[Am]Six of them in [F]Tirzah he held the [G]land
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
He saw a [F]hill that [G]needed a [C]name
And he saw a [F]price that [G]would be [Am]paid
Two [F]talents of [G]silver he [Am]gave
To the [F]owner of the [G]hill in the [C]valley
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He [F]bought the hill [G]of Samaria
[C]From Shemer the owner [Am]of the land
He [F]built a city [G]on the stone
And named it after the [C]man he found
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
But Om[G/B]ri did evil in the [Am]Lord's sight
[F]More wicked than [G]all who went [C]before
[F]He followed the [G]path of Jer[C]oboam
And led [F]Israel away from the [G]door
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
With worthless [F]idols [G]they pro[C]voked
The God [F]of Is[G]rael to be [Am]angry
They [F]followed the [G]sin of the [Am]king
And [F]turned their [G]hearts to vani[C]ty
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He [F]bought the hill [G]of Samaria
From [C]Shemer the owner of the [Am]land
He built a [F]city on the [G]stone
And named it after the man he [C]found
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
The book of the kings [G/B]records his [Am]acts
The ex[F]ploits he per[G]formed are [C]known
But [F]Omri rest[G]ed with his [C]fathers
[Am]And was [F]buried in the [G]city a[C]lone
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
His son A[F]hab became [G]king in his [C]place
And the [F]story of [G]Israel continued [C]on [F][G][C]
{end_of_verse}
